{
  "about": [
    "Agility obstacles, by course. Each obstacle: key, loc (type id), option (the start of the loc's option text), level, xpTenths, at ([x, z, level], only when several locs of one type are different obstacles), routes, and for one that can fail success ([low, high] out of 256, guessed: the Wiki gives no fail rates) and damage ([min, max]).",
    "A route: from ([x, z, level], where the player starts; the nearest route is taken), moves, and fail (the moves of a failure, for an obstacle that can fail).",
    "Moves, in order: anim (anim, ticks: plays it and waits), teleport (to: straight there, another level too), walk (path of [x, z] turning points, anim: one tile a tick through anything, with anim as the whole stance), slide (to, anim, startCycles, endCycles, ticks: the client's exact move; client cycles are 20 ms, 30 a tick).",
    "Courses: key, obstacles (their keys in order), lapXpTenths (on top of the last obstacle's; 0 for the rooftops, whose last obstacle holds the lap's) and lapLine (the lap count message's key); for marks of grace also level (the course's Agility level), marks (the [x, z, level] tiles a mark lands on) and markChance ([numerator, denominator] a lap). An obstacle may name its own levelLine.", "Marks of grace: the chance a lap (2/6 on every course here) and the spots from the OSRS Wiki's Mark of Grace page and its Mark of grace spawns table (read 2026-11-02); Draynor's: the roofs of the start, Diango's Workshop, the Slayer shop and Ned's rope shop.",
    "Draynor Village Rooftop Course: locs, tiles and options from the 241 cache's map (the roofs are the level 3 tiles with floor); levels and XP from the OSRS Wiki (read 2026-11-02, after the 8 May 2024 rework: level 1, nothing fails). Inferred from the map: each start, path and landing tile. Guessed until recorded: the animations (by their cache names), every tick count and exact move timing."
  ],
